<title>USA: Three bidders line up for U.S. Stockpile germanium.</title>
<headline>Three bidders line up for U.S. Stockpile germanium.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three bidders emerged to make offers for U.S. Stockpile's surplus germanium metal.</p>
<p>Tennelec/Nucleus Inc bid for 17 kilograms at a unit price of $1,200 a kilogram.</p>
<p>PPM Pure Metals Gmbh bid for 2,000 kilos of germanium at $980 to $1,260 a kilo.</p>
<p>Meldform Germanium Ltd bid for 500 kilos at $803 a kilo.</p>
<p>Outcome of the offering was due soon.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
</text>
